This Python program initializes a 4-wire PWM fan connected to GPIO12 using the gpiozero library. It also sets up a Picamera2 for video capture and an MQTT client for receiving fan speed commands. The program continuously prompts the user for a fan speed percentage or exits with a 'q' command. It handles invalid inputs and keyboard interrupts gracefully. If hardware PWM is unavailable, it falls back to software PWM. The program ensures that all resources are released cleanly on exit.

